# AXIS CELL: scrutinee type = ENUM with COMPLETE top-level coverage and ALL
# IRREFUTABLE sub-patterns x consumer = the DIVERGENCE gate. Its join-site twin
# is `match_exhaustive_no_catchall_join_reject.gg`.
#
# ⚠ THIS CELL PINS A KNOWN FALSE POSITIVE, not a bug being fixed. No value of
# `Tag` skips this `match` and every arm `return`s, so `print(s)` is genuinely
# unreachable and the program is memory-safe. Both compilers reject it anyway,
# because both classify fall-through SYNTACTICALLY (an `else`/catch-all arm) and
# neither consults an exhaustiveness verdict here. The self-host is wired to the
# CURRENT behaviour deliberately, so the regression cannot silently flip.
#
# GRADUATION: when the precise rule lands -- a SECOND verdict bit recording
# IRREFUTABLE coverage, which is a new design with its own gauntlet -- this cell
# MOVES to `self_host_driver_accepts_liveness` and its `known_gaps` repro
# `tests/fixtures/known_gaps/sh_exhaustive_match_not_credited_as_diverging.gg`
# graduates with it. The bare exhaustiveness verdict the typechecker already
# computes is NOT that bit: it credits a REFUTABLE nested sub-pattern as full
# coverage (see the `TODO.md` entry beginning "`collect_covered_variants` counts
# a REFUTABLE NESTED SUB-PATTERN"), so fusing it in would accept a real
# use-after-move -- which is exactly what
# `match_nested_refutable_diverge_use_after_move_reject.gg` catches.
#
# RED-VERIFY (pre-fix HEAD): ACCEPTED, rc 0, 5237 bytes of C.
enum Tag:
    A(int)
    B(int)

void sink(String ^x):
    pass

void probe(Tag g, bool c):
    String s = "hello"
    if c:
        sink(^s)
        match g:
            case Tag.A(_):
                return
            case Tag.B(_):
                return
    print(s)

void main():
    probe(Tag.A(1), true)
